  "text_md": "<!-- image -->\n\nCorrigendum\n\nCorrigendum to ' Midwifery continuity of carer in an area of high socioeconomic disadvantage in London: A retrospective analysis of Albany Midwifery Practice outcomes using routine data (1997 -2009) ' [Midwifery 48 (2017) 1 -10]\n\nCaroline S.E. Homer, RM, MMed(ClinEpi), PhD Professor a, ⁎ , Nicky Leap, DMid Adjunct Professor of Midwifery a , Nadine Edwards, PhD Independent Researcher a,b,c , Jane Sandall, PhD, CBE Professor, NIHR Senior Investigator b,c\n\na Centre for Midwifery, Child and Family Health, Faculty of Health, University of Technology Sydney, PO Box 123, Broadway, Sydney, New South Wales 2007, Australia\n\nb Division of Women's Health, Faculty of Life Sciences &amp; Medicine, King's College London, United Kingdom\n\nc Women's Health Academic Centre, St. Thomas' Hospital, London SE1 7EH, United Kingdom\n\nThe authors regret that on page 8 we inadvertently referred to NICE as providing policy and policy direction. This was incorrect. NICE provides national clinical guidance based on systematic reviews. The sentence should read: A large study comparing perinatal outcomes by planned place of birth (Birthplace in England Collaborative Group, 2011) supported the clinical guidance to o ff er women with low risk pregnancies a choice of birth settings, including birth at home (NICE, 2014).\n\nThe authors would like to apologise for any inconvenience caused.\n\n[DOI of original article: http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.02.009](http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.02.009)\n\n⁎ Corresponding author.\n\nE-mail address: caroline.homer@uts.edu.au (C.S.E. Homer).\n\n[http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013](http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013)\n\n0266-6138/ © 2017 The Author(s). Published by Elsevier Ltd. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/BY-NC-ND/4.0/).\n\n## ARTICLE IN PRESS\n\n[Midwifery xxx (xxxx) xxx-xxx](http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013)\n\nContents lists available at ScienceDirect\n\n## Midwifery\n\njournal homepage: www.elsevier.com/locate/midw\n\n<!-- image -->",
